A_PROGRAM_ARTIFACT 84

This file is the canonical semantic manifest for artifact version 84. The
artifact header carries the SHA-256 digest of these exact bytes. A reader must
reject a different version or digest before reading the interface. Version 83
is not accepted and has no compatibility parser. Version 84 replaces generic
reachable-obligation export fallback with exact accepted or conditional
evidence and adds canonical occurrence-to-obligation dependency edges.
Effect rows and occurrence classifier closure remain orthogonal.

The header is followed by one immutable Intrinsic-environment contract:

intrinsic_environment FINGERPRINT DEFAULT_INTEGER_HOST_TYPE

FINGERPRINT is the deterministic 64-bit identity of namespace bindings, pure
primitive signatures, effect-operation signatures, and the default unsuffixed
integer representation. DEFAULT_INTEGER_HOST_TYPE must agree with that
fingerprint. Read and link reject an environment mismatch before interpreting
literal or primitive Claims. In the default environment, Int and Int32 name
HOST_TYPE_INT32 and unsuffixed integer literals have exactly that principal;
Int64 remains distinct. INT_LITERAL_ADMISSIBILITY is retained in the numeric
wire vocabulary only as a reserved historical ordinal and is not emitted or
accepted by the v84 compiler.

The artifact is one dense accepted object graph. Every section uses IDs in
0..count-1 with no holes. Solver candidates, work queues, HOTT actions,
bridges, certificates, normalization fuel, graph revisions, and closure ranks
are compiler-local and absent.

judgement_kind UNKNOWN=0 HAS_TYPE=1 IS_TYPE=2
judgement_authority INVALID=0 TYPED_OCCURRENCE=1 CONTEXT_BINDING=2 TYPE_DECLARATION=3 INTRINSIC=4 TYPE_FORMATION=5 UNIVERSE=6 CORE_HELPER=7 EXPORT=8
judgement_proof INVALID=0 TYPE_FORMATION_INTRO=1 CONSTRUCTOR_INTRO=2 CONSTRUCTOR_SPINE_FORMATION=3 BINDER_ASSUMPTION=4 MATCH_PATTERN_ASSUMPTION=5 LAMBDA_INTRO=6 APP_ELIM=7 RETURN_INTRO=8 THUNK_INTRO=9 FORCE_ELIM=10 OPERATION_REQUEST_INTRO=11 COMPUTATION_FOLD_ELIM=12 MATCH_TYPE_FORMATION_INTRO=13 MATCH_ELIM=14 SOLVED_MATCH_MOTIVE=15 INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS_ELIM=16 TEXT_LITERAL_INTRO=17 PURE_PRIMITIVE_TYPE_INTRO=18 EFFECT_OPERATION_TYPE_INTRO=19 CONVERSION=20 EXPECTED_TYPE_EXPOSURE=21 TEXT_TYPE_INTRO=22 INT_LITERAL_INTRO=23 INT_LITERAL_ADMISSIBILITY=24 INT_TYPE_INTRO=25 HOST_TYPE_INTRO=26 IS_TYPE_FROM_HAS_TYPE=27 DECLARATION=28 UNIVERSE_CUMULATIVITY=29 PI_FORMATION_INTRO=30 CONTEXT_WEAKEN=31 EFFECT_WEAKEN=32 SUBSTITUTION_REINDEX=35 COMPUTATION_TYPE_FORMATION=43 THUNK_TYPE_FORMATION=44 DIMENSION_ACTION_TYPE_FORMATION=45 DIMENSION_ACTION_TERM=46 DIMENSION_ACTION_CONSTRUCTOR=47 DIMENSION_ACTION_THUNK_RETURN_WITNESS=48 TERMINATES_TYPE_FORMATION=51 TERMINATES_TOTAL_COMPUTATION=54 STATIC_FAMILY_APP_ELIM=55

Compiler-local relation-action proof kinds 33,34,36,37,38,39,40,41,42 are
not accepted wire proof kinds. SUBSTITUTION_REINDEX=35 is object evidence for
a Context/Substitution action and is intentionally retained.

term_tag VAR=1 CONSTRUCTOR=2 APP=3 LAMBDA=4 PI=5 MATCH=6 TYPE_FORMER=7 TYPE_DECLARATION=8 INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS=9 UNIVERSE_VAR=10 PRIMITIVE_TEXT=11 TEXT_LITERAL=12 PRIMITIVE_INT=13 PRIMITIVE_INT64=14 INT_LITERAL=15 EXTERNAL_REF=16 PURE_PRIMITIVE=17 EFFECT_OPERATION=18 TYPE_VIEW=19 EFFECT_ROW_EMPTY=20 EFFECT_ROW_VAR=21 EFFECT_ROW_UNION=22 EFFECT_ROW_FORALL=23 COMPUTATION_TYPE=24 THUNK_TYPE=25 RETURN=26 THUNK=27 FORCE=28 OPERATION_REQUEST=29 COMPUTATION_FOLD=30 EFFECT_ROW_OPERATION=31 DIMENSION_ACTION=34 TERMINATES_TYPE_FORMER=37 TERMINATES_WITNESS_FORMER=38
computation_totality UNKNOWN=0 TOTAL=1 MAY_DIVERGE=2

COMPUTATION_TYPE serializes EFFECT_LABEL, RESULT_TYPE, and TOTALITY. TOTALITY
must be TOTAL or MAY_DIVERGE. UNKNOWN is a compiler-local unresolved solver
state and is rejected on publication and readback; it is never an object-term
classifier. Joining computations preserves MAY_DIVERGE if either operand may
diverge, preserves TOTAL only when both operands are total, and otherwise
remains compiler-local UNKNOWN.

Compiler-local RELATION_TYPE_FORMER=32 and
RELATION_WITNESS_FORMER=33 are not accepted identity-root syntax.

DIMENSION_ACTION serializes SOURCE_TERM, SOURCE_DIMENSION, TARGET_DIMENSION,
IMAGE_COUNT, and exactly IMAGE_COUNT pairs of IMAGE_KIND and TARGET_AXIS.
IMAGE_COUNT equals SOURCE_DIMENSION. Readback interns this canonical operator
tuple and stores only the resulting operator ID in memory; compiler-local
operator IDs are never wire authority.

TERMINATES_TYPE_FORMER and TERMINATES_WITNESS_FORMER are fieldless heads of
one-argument APP spines. `Terminates(c)` is derivable only from an accepted
`Thunk(Comp(E,A,TOTAL))` classifier. E may be nonempty. This proposition does
not alter DefEq or infer termination from effect-row emptiness.

type_expr_tag UNIVERSE=1 UNIVERSE_VAR=2 SELF=3 VAR=4 NAME=5 APP=6 ARROW=7 PI=8 IMPORTED_TYPE=9 EXTERNAL_TERM=10 PRIMITIVE_TEXT=11 PRIMITIVE_INT=12 PRIMITIVE_INT64=13 LOCAL_TYPE_MEMBER=14
typed_occurrence_kind ATOM=1 VAR=2 REFERENCE=3 CONSTRUCTOR=4 APP=5 LAMBDA=6 MATCH=7 INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS=8 EXPECTED_TYPE=9 RETURN=10 THUNK=11 FORCE=12 REQUEST=13 COMPUTATION_FOLD=14
typed_occurrence_category INVALID=0 VALUE=1 COMPUTATION=2 TYPE=3
typed_occurrence_application_role NONE=0 FUNCTION_ELIMINATION=1 CONSTRUCTOR_FORMATION=2 PURE_TYPE_FAMILY_EVALUATION=3
typed_occurrence_classifier_status PENDING=0 SOLVED=1 RESIDUAL_VERIFICATION=2
substitution_kind IDENTITY=1 EMPTY=2 PROJECTION=3 EXTEND=4 COMPOSE=5
verification_kind COMPUTATION_FOLD_RESULT=1 EFFECT_ROW_EQUATION=2
verification_state PENDING=1 DISCHARGED=2 FAILED=3
effect_constraint_kind EXACT=1 COPY=2 UNION=3 RESIDUAL=4
normalization_profile CORE_WHNF=1 COMPUTATION_WHNF=2 PURE_TYPE_WHNF=3
term_export_evidence ACCEPTED_CLAIM=1 CONDITIONAL=2
export_transparency OPAQUE=1 TRANSPARENT=2
compile_policy STRICT=1 HYBRID=2 EXPLORATORY=3
definition_thunk_policy IMPLICIT=1 EXPLICIT=2
identity_computation_rule INVALID=0 ORDINARY_ADT=1 THUNK_RETURN=2 PI_POINTWISE=3 GENERIC_DIMENSION_ACTION=5
usage_grade ZERO=0 ONE=1 MANY=2
universe_node TYPE=1 PARAMETER=2
universe_edge PARAMETER_TO_TYPE=1
universe_reason INVALID=0 TERM_LEVEL_SUCCESSOR=1 PI_DOMAIN=2 PI_CODOMAIN=3 MATCH_BRANCH=4 APP_CUMULATIVITY=5 EXPECTED_TYPE_CUMULATIVITY=6 DERIVED_UNIVERSE_LEVEL=7 DERIVED_PI_DOMAIN=8 DERIVED_PI_CODOMAIN=9

Interface identity root:
identity_root ID SOURCE_TYPE_CLAIM IDENTITY_FAMILY_HAS_TYPE_CLAIM WITNESS_HAS_TYPE_CLAIM_OR_INVALID COMPUTATION_RULE

The mandatory source Claim proves that the source carrier is a type. The
mandatory family Claim classifies an ordinary computed identity family by the
same admitted Universe. The optional witness Claim classifies an ordinary
proof Term by exactly that family. The computation rule must be replayed from
the source Claim, the canonical dimension operator embedded in the acted Term,
the acted-family Claim, and the witness Claim; the root label is not authority
by itself. Exact duplicate quadruples are rejected. Registration is permitted
only after accepted-graph publication is frozen. Roots never add conversion
equations or equality reflection.

The dependency table is recomputed from the final dense rooted publication
graph. External references reachable only through accepted proof premises,
rule payloads, Contexts, or Substitutions are dependencies. External references
present only in unrooted solver or HOTT work are not dependencies.

Dense accepted proof grammar:
propositions N
proposition ID KIND AUTHORITY_KIND AUTHORITY_ID CONTEXT OCCURRENCE SUBJECT CLASSIFIER USAGE_COUNT [BINDING_ID USAGE_GRADE]*
claims N
claim ID proposition PROPOSITION_ID
derivations N
derivation ID PROOF_KIND claim CONCLUSION_CLAIM premises PREMISE_COUNT
payload none
| payload constructor OWNER_VIEW CONSTRUCTOR_INDEX FIELD_INDEX
| payload constructor_spine OWNER_VIEW
| payload induction MATCH MOTIVE CASE_INDEX FIELD_INDEX
action SEMANTIC_ACTION_KIND SEMANTIC_ACTION_ID
premise claim CLAIM_ID action SEMANTIC_ACTION_KIND SEMANTIC_ACTION_ID
| premise scoped PROPOSITION_ID action SEMANTIC_ACTION_KIND SEMANTIC_ACTION_ID

MATCH_PATTERN_ASSUMPTION uses constructor payload.
CONSTRUCTOR_SPINE_FORMATION uses constructor_spine payload.
INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS_ELIM uses induction payload.
Every other admitted proof kind uses none payload.
Exactly one premise reference is valid. Proposition identity is serialized
once; Claims and scoped premises refer to it directly. Derivation sources are
exactly the ordered premise edges and are not repeated in a sources list.

Resource usage is part of Proposition identity. Usage entries are strictly
increasing persistent Context binding IDs; ZERO entries are omitted. ONE is
one use and MANY is the saturated image of every count greater than one.
Sequential composition uses saturated addition, mutually exclusive branches
use maximum, and substitution multiplies each target grade by the usage vector
of its source assignment before adding columns. Projection weakening preserves
the vector because persistent binding IDs remain stable. Thunk is
grade-preserving and never grants contraction to a captured resource or
resumption. Until object-identity Context bridges carry an explicit graded
modality, an object-term action with nonempty resource usage is residual.

Type declarations serialize only named source or imported schemas: namespace,
name, parameter and index Contexts, index count, constructor telescope, result
classifier, and optional readback/cache data. Every declaration has a name.
Computed identity and higher-dimensional families are DIMENSION_ACTION Terms,
not anonymous declarations. No declaration origin or generated carrier field
exists in v84.

type_declarations N
type_decl ID NAME NAMESPACE TYPE_INDEX FIRST_PARAMETER PARAMETER_COUNT FIRST_CONSTRUCTOR CONSTRUCTOR_COUNT FORMATION_CLASSIFIER PARAMETER_CONTEXT INDEX_CONTEXT INDEX_COUNT

NAME is mandatory. NAMESPACE may be `-` for the root namespace. TYPE_INDEX
equals ID. Every referenced Context, constructor range, parameter range, and
formation classifier must be present in the same dense object graph.

All object graph arenas are dense. Solver variables, worklists, source AST
node IDs, source AST binder IDs, runtime environments, normalization caches,
and duplicate Core child columns are absent. Closure rank and lookup indices
are reconstructed by least-fixed-point replay after readback.

Typed occurrence grammar:
compile_policy POLICY THUNK_POLICY ENTRY_NAME_OR_DASH ENTRY_TERM_OR_INVALID ENTRY_CLASSIFIER_OR_INVALID ENTRY_OCCURRENCE_OR_INVALID REQUIRED_RUNTIME_CAPABILITIES
contexts N
context ID PARENT BINDING CLASSIFIER EXTENSION_KIND SOURCE_COMPUTATION_OR_INVALID DEPTH
typed_occurrences N
typed_occurrence ID KIND CATEGORY APPLICATION_ROLE CORE_TERM CLASSIFIER_STATUS CLASSIFIER_OR_INVALID VERIFICATION_OBLIGATION_OR_INVALID SOURCE_NAME_OR_DASH BINDER_NAME_OR_DASH BINDING_ID_OR_INVALID WRAPPED_OCCURRENCE_OR_INVALID BINDER_CLASSIFIER_OR_INVALID IH_OWNER_OCCURRENCE_OR_INVALID IH_SCOPE_OR_INVALID IH_CASE_OR_INVALID IH_FIELD_OR_INVALID FOLD_RETURN_BINDING_OR_INVALID IMPLICIT_ROW_COUNT FIRST_CASE_OR_INVALID CASE_COUNT FIRST_FOLD_CLAUSE_OR_INVALID FOLD_CLAUSE_COUNT CONTEXT CONTEXT_ACTION_SUBSTITUTION_OR_INVALID SOURCE_CORE_TERM_OR_INVALID SOURCE_CLASSIFIER_OR_INVALID
typed_occurrence_rows ID [BINDING_ID]*
occurrence_edges N
occurrence_edge ID PARENT_OCCURRENCE CHILD_ROLE ORDINAL CHILD_OCCURRENCE
occurrence_fold_clauses N
occurrence_fold_clause ID CONTEXT ARGUMENT_BINDING CONTINUATION_BINDING
occurrence_match_cases N
occurrence_match_case ID CONTEXT REFINEMENT_STATUS REFINEMENT_SUBSTITUTION_OR_INVALID CONSTRUCTOR_OWNER CONSTRUCTOR_ID LABEL_OR_DASH
occurrence_match_case_binders ID BINDER_COUNT [BINDING_ID]*

REFINEMENT_STATUS is SOLVED (1), IMPOSSIBLE (2), or CONSTANT (4). SOLVED
requires one refinement Substitution whose source is the stored branch
Context. IMPOSSIBLE and CONSTANT require INVALID substitution. CONSTANT means
that the index equation remained residual but the accepted Match motive does
not use the refined index; it is not a solved equation. Compiler-workspace
PENDING (0) and RESIDUAL (3) states are rejected at publication and readback.

Occurrence edges are the only typed-layer correspondence topology. APP,
Lambda, Match, CBPV, request, and computation-fold children are not repeated
in occurrence records or side tables; their computational topology belongs to
TermDB. Match and fold side tables retain only information that is not
recoverable from alpha-shared Core nodes: refined Contexts, constructor
selection, and persistent occurrence Binding identities.

EXTENSION_KIND is INVALID (0) only for the empty Context, VALUE (1) for an
ordinary value assumption, or SEQUENCE_RESULT (2) for the value delivered to a
sequencing continuation. SEQUENCE_RESULT names the raw source computation Term
and is relocated, closed, and replayed with the Context.

Term export grammar:
term_exports N
term NAME LOCAL_TERM CLASSIFIER TRANSPARENCY CANONICAL_KEY CLASSIFIER_KEY
  namespace NAMESPACE occurrence OCCURRENCE evidence KIND ID CONDITION_COUNT
  [OBLIGATION_ID]*

ACCEPTED_CLAIM evidence has CONDITION_COUNT zero and ID is the exact accepted
HAS_TYPE Claim for the exported occurrence, subject, classifier, and Context.
CONDITIONAL evidence has nonzero CONDITION_COUNT. ID is either the exact
accepted HAS_TYPE Claim for the exported occurrence, subject, classifier, and
Context, or INVALID only when one exact classifier-closing residual obligation
is the base evidence. In v84 that exceptional base is a
COMPUTATION_FOLD_RESULT whose kind descriptor permits later Claim
reconstruction; an EFFECT_ROW_EQUATION can never be the base typing evidence.
An occurrence may already have a SOLVED classifier while a distinct pending
COMPUTATION_FOLD_RESULT still guards its accepted typing Claim. In that case
the serialized classifier must equal the occurrence classifier and the exact
fold-result condition remains mandatory.
The following obligation IDs are strictly increasing. Their interface-local
offset is reconstructed in memory and is not wire authority. A reader
recomputes the condition set from the frozen occurrence graph and dependency
edge table and requires exact equality, rejecting missing and extra
conditions.

After constructor exports, `function_graph_associations COUNT` contains dense
records `function_graph_association ID OWNER_TERM_EXPORT GRAPH_TYPE_EXPORT
RESULT_TYPE_EXPORT GRAPH_INTERFACE_TERM_EXPORT CERTIFIED_ADAPTER_TERM_EXPORT
CERTIFIED_RUNNER_TERM_EXPORT CERTIFIED_ARGUMENT_INDEX`. The owner, graph,
result, interface, and runner exports must be present and each owner occurs at
most once. `GRAPH_INTERFACE_TERM_EXPORT` is the type-level eta bridge that
suspends the generated family when it is passed as a CBPV value.
`CERTIFIED_ADAPTER_TERM_EXPORT` is `4294967295` unless the owner has a generated
binary-Bool adapter into the common callback package.
`CERTIFIED_ARGUMENT_INDEX` is `4294967295` for a first-order owner; otherwise it
identifies the raw higher-order argument followed by the graph interface and
certified callback in the generated families and runner. Link and replay never
reconstruct this ownership relation from Core equality.

In first-order mode the owner is the evidence-erasing projection of the
certified runner and has the same callable argument spine. A generated adapter,
when present, has the same owner argument spine and changes only the result
package. In higher-order mode the raw owner remains the executable definition:
changing its ABI would require every caller to provide graph evidence for its
callback. The certified runner is a distinct, additional variant. At
CERTIFIED_ARGUMENT_INDEX it may expose the suspended raw callback as its
callable Pi spine; immediately after it the runner accepts a callback graph
family with the same input spine plus one output index and a certified callback
with the same input spine. This is the CBPV callable exposure, not generic
Core-shape equivalence.

Readers validate the selected mode, accepted classifiers, TypeView-preserving
binder-aware owner/runner domains, exact graph/result family heads, the
two-field result package, callback package shape, adapter ABI, and relocated
association again after graph append. The graph-interface export must contain
an instance of the designated graph family, and the runner result must be an
instance of the designated result family. Generated names remain diagnostics,
not semantic evidence. The association does not claim that raw higher-order
execution is certified.

A frozen occurrence has exactly one closure state. SOLVED names one present
classifier and has no verification obligation. RESIDUAL_VERIFICATION has no
classifier and names one persisted pending obligation. PENDING is a compiler
workspace state and is rejected by publication and readback.

Normalization and solver budgets, consumed steps, worklist state, solved
constraint counts, and effect-constraint diagnostic snapshots are compiler
session state. They are not serialized. Any deferred semantic requirement is
represented only by a versioned verification obligation and an explicit
occurrence dependency edge. `classifier_verification_obligation` remains
exclusive to classifier closure and is not an effect-condition reference.

Verification grammar:
verification_obligations N
verification ID KIND STATE OCCURRENCE CORE_TERM COMPUTATION_OCCURRENCE
  CONTINUATION_OCCURRENCE CONTINUATION_BINDING INPUT_CLASSIFIER
  CLASSIFIER_FAMILY EFFECT_ROW EFFECT_CONSTRAINT_KIND NORMALIZATION_PROFILE
  SCHEMA_VERSION
verification_dependencies N
verification_dependency ID OCCURRENCE OBLIGATION_ID

Dependency records are sorted by `(OCCURRENCE, OBLIGATION_ID)`, contain no
duplicates, and target only PENDING obligations. In the v84 initial fragment
each residual has its exact source edge. Conditional-use propagation is not
silently approximated: a source consumer that would require a propagated
condition is rejected until that propagation rule is implemented.

A typed occurrence carries the action triple
CONTEXT_ACTION_SUBSTITUTION, SOURCE_CORE_TERM, SOURCE_CLASSIFIER. All three are
INVALID for an untransformed source occurrence, or all three are valid. For a
transformed occurrence the Substitution source is the occurrence Context;
SOURCE_CORE_TERM and SOURCE_CLASSIFIER must both be reindexable through that
Substitution, and the projected source term must be CORE_TERM. The projected
source classifier is pullback-time evidence: the final structural classifier
may be refined later by constraint solving, so equality with the final
classifier is not required. Keeping this triple is necessary to reconstruct
typed evidence after indexed branch pullback without treating shared Core Term
identity as occurrence identity.

Each Match-case binder entry stores only its authoritative persistent Binding
ID. Replay does not assume that case binders are the final Context extensions:
indexed pullback may retain free branch variables after the constructor
telescope.

Each typed-occurrence Substitution record ends with an evidence Claim ID.
IDENTITY, EMPTY, PROJECTION, and COMPOSE use INVALID. EXTEND must name the exact
accepted HAS_TYPE Claim for its source Context, assigned Term, and reindexed
classifier. The Claim must have an accepted Derivation. This compact edge is
wire authority because those four fields need not identify a unique Claim when
different source authorities prove the same proposition.

Observational identity fragment admitted by roots:
- homogeneous ordinary ADT identity families represented by one-dimensional
  DIMENSION_ACTION terms and ordinary constructor witnesses checked against
  their acted schemas;
- repeated generic dimension actions whose canonical operator extends the
  source dimension by one and whose complete boundary is replayable;
- pure Return/Thunk identity families represented by dimension action and
  constructor witnesses; and
- nondependent pure Pi pointwise identity families and ordinary Lambda/Match
  witnesses whose complete accepted derivation graph replays read-only.

No fixed square constructor generator or generated declaration is admitted.
Dimensions one, two, and higher use the same operator/action representation.
Contextual actions are publishable only when their complete ordinary
Context/Claim/Derivation evidence is reachable from a semantic root.

These roots certify only the explicitly listed type-directed computation and
inhabitance rules. They do not turn compiler-local RELATION_TYPE or TERM action
results into identity, and they do not claim completeness for contextual
equivalence. Dependent constructor fields, general dependent APP/Match/IH
action, and generic lifting through an index telescope remain residual.

Universe action, full Universe bisimulation/coherence, generic transport,
effectful requests/folds, host primitives, HIT, quotient, and general IADT
identity computation remain residual and cannot be roots.

Dependent computation-fold verification lifecycle:
- a fold whose result family closes by deterministic pure normalization may
  contribute ordinary static typing evidence;
- blocked-effect or exhausted pure normalization creates one versioned
  COMPUTATION_FOLD_RESULT obligation keyed by the typed occurrence;
- a PENDING computation-fold obligation is a runtime contract and never a
  Claim or Derivation;
- strict compilation and Verilog admission reject PENDING obligations;
- hybrid compilation may publish PENDING obligations only when the selected
  backend declares the computation-fold result verifier and handler
  capabilities;
- artifact v84 persists only PENDING obligations. DISCHARGED and FAILED are
  execution-instance outcomes and are rejected on readback;
- execution discharges an obligation by applying its retained pure classifier
  family to the returned value and checking conversion with the continuation
  result classifier under the retained normalization profile; and
- failed discharge aborts that execution and cannot retroactively create or
  alter accepted static evidence.

An unresolved effect equation is persisted as an EFFECT_ROW_EQUATION
obligation containing its exact constraint kind, occurrence, and result and
operand rows. This immutable contract replaces the compiler-local mutable
effect-constraint snapshot. Compile/link discharge must use canonical row
normal forms; naming a host is not discharge evidence. Successful equation
checking removes only the dependency edge. It does not fabricate a HAS_TYPE
Claim: ordinary candidate reconstruction and accepted replay are independently
required. Host discharge is not part of v84. An effect obligation is never an
accepted typing Claim by itself.
Contextual equivalence is a metatheoretic adequacy target, not an artifact
record or kernel proof-search rule.

Recursive Match frame grammar:
match_frames N
match_frame ID MATCH_TERM SCRUTINEE_BINDING_OR_INVALID CASE_COUNT IS_LINKABLE MATCH_KEY

SCRUTINEE_BINDING_OR_INVALID is the persistent BindingId of the recursive
Match subject when that subject is a variable. It is not a display name or a
de Bruijn position. Branch substitution preserves this binding until iota
reduction, where the current recursive scrutinee is substituted into it before
constructor-field binders. This is runtime semantics and therefore wire
authority; reconstructing it from an alpha-interned Match after readback is
not permitted. The referenced Match scrutinee must be a VAR whose persistent
BindingId is exactly SCRUTINEE_BINDING_OR_INVALID; missing, merely in-range,
or different bindings are rejected.
